fundamentals
- Original 1609 grant ran 200 miles north and south of Point Comfort, then west "from sea to sea"
- Western claims were paper titles overlapping other colonies and later federal land policy
- Shrinkage came from cessions to Congress, new-state formation, and wartime secession of western counties
- Final 1863 outline is the Virginia that remains today

sequence
1609  vast sea-to-sea claim
1784  Midwest ceded
1792  Kentucky gone
1863  West Virginia split off

